<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 14.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - March 14.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 03/14/97  03/07/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     21.40     29.94     9.20	12.88	8.1</p>
<p>West	     50.10     56.72    19.33	21.89     27.4</p>
<p>Total Canada   71.50     86.67    14.54	17.63     18.2</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 03/14/97: 232.55 bcf, 03/07/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 03/14/97: 259.11 bcf, 03/07/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
